The end of the orcish rogue story...

As he survived some minor dumb moves quite unimpressed, he continued his
run to the planes.  He even left back 80k+ of gold to get unburdened!
No worthy rogue would do that, of course, so his fate was determined.
And where is the best place to die?  On the astral planes, only few steps
away from glory immortality.  What happened was the usual avoidable stupid
death.

Already finished Famine two times with an instant working wand.  Many more
angelics and priests fell by some corpse of a-stone-ishment.  Pestillence
was the next rider.  Why zapping that wand when having that corpse at hand?
There is at least on reason, you might tell me.  And you would be correct.

Surprised by the non-effective corpse attack, the irrationalities begun.
He became deathly sick.  Then instead of acting, he first switched weapon.
Then he noticed being burdened, he dropped the bag.  Then he applied the
unicorn horn twice with no effect.  Then he looted the bag to get potions
of full healing.  Then he died.  Then he quaffed the potions.  Then...

Umm, well, nearly so.  The above causality problem terminated his life.

Leaving some recharged wands of death on the planes (Death will surely
have some use for these), some amulets of life saving, an unused wand
of wishing, two magic lamps, a lot of rusty, diluted, blank stuff, and
these trusty 12 +7 daggers he started with.

No condolence, no recommendations for better tactics, no flames, please.
The next orc is on the way  :-)

